1) Explain what exactly is notification system.
Notification system is a system which takes notification from different services and send it to different users depending upon the medium of the user , by using
which the user want to receive the notification.

2)Ask clarifying questions and then give functional and non functional requirements.
So , in notification system , functional requirements include that client should be able to get notification depening upon the priority of the notification .ie.
if it is otp (one time password) , then it is of high priority , and it should be given to client with minimum latency , but if it is advertisement notification ,
then latency is allowed . Rate limiting is also very important from client and server side , that how many times client can send the messages to server ,and how many
times the server can send messages to client. Non functional requirements include high availability and very low latency. and it should be scalable.

3)Back of the envelope estimation.
Let's suppose there are 1 million people using the notification system , and 1 person recieves 10 notifications . then total notifications will be 10 million.
so , per second , the number of notifications which will be received to the user is 10 million/(total number of second in a day). and if each notification store 
5 MB , then total storage for 5 years will be (5 years)*(5 MB)*( 10 million/(total number of second in a day) ) .

